+# Design: Move off left-pad
+
+Ecosystem: JavaScript (CommonJS project). Version in use: 1.3.0 (latest is also 1.3.0).
+
+## Approach
+
+Replace calls to `left-pad` with a project-owned, dependency-free module `src/vendor/left-pad.js` that is built on `String.prototype.padStart` and keeps the answers of `left-pad` for every case the séance compares. No package is added to the runtime dependencies.
+
+A bare `padStart` swap is not safe (see "Known behavioural differences"), so the module is a small wrapper, not a direct call. The generated bundle's replacement (`seance/left-pad/replacement.mjs`, an ES module) is the source; the project is CommonJS, so the same function lives in `src/vendor/left-pad.js` as CommonJS (`module.exports = leftPad; module.exports.leftPad = leftPad;`) and the séance imports it with `import mod from '../../src/vendor/left-pad.js'`. The generated spec names no `.ts` path; the project's language is JavaScript.
+
+## Where it is used
+
+`src/receipt.js` only: one `require('left-pad')` and 4 calls (lines 34, 44, 45, 51), with 2 or 3 arguments. `options.fill` reaches two of the calls unchanged, so an empty or multi-character fill is possible in production.
+
+## The séance (differential test)
+
+A curated recipe (`left-pad`) wrote it; it was run against the real packages before it was shipped. For the default export the test:
+
+1. draws the text from strings, numbers, null, undefined and booleans; the length from integers, fractions, numeric strings, NaN and infinities; the fill from empty, multi-character and non-string values;
+2. calls `left-pad` and the replacement with the same input;
+3. fails if the results differ, or if exactly one of them throws a different class of error, and shows the shrunk input and both answers.
+
+Files added to the project:
+
+- `seance/left-pad/seance.test.mjs` (test)
+- `seance/left-pad/replacement.mjs` (the bundle's replacement; the séance's import line is changed to point at `src/vendor/left-pad.js` once that file exists)
+- `seance/left-pad/README.md` (readme)
+
+Install and run (the tool's install command lists only the test tooling; `left-pad` stays installed while the project still declares it):
+
+```sh
+npm install --save-dev vitest fast-check
+npx vitest run seance/left-pad
+```
+
+What it compares and ignores:
+
+- The returned string, or the error class when the call throws (never the message).
+- Strings, numbers, null, undefined and booleans as the text; lengths that are integers, fractions, numeric strings, NaN and infinities; empty, multi-character and non-string fill characters.
+- Not compared: lengths of 2^31 or more (left-pad wraps them around).
+- The project's own calls (`projectCalls` in the séance) are extra examples. The scan keeps only literal arguments.
+
+Vitest needs Node 22.12 or newer; the project declares `engines.node >=18`. The production code does not need Vitest; only the séance does. The project's `npm test` uses `node --test`, which would pick up the Vitest file, so `test` names its own files (`node --test test/*.test.js`) and a separate `seance` script runs Vitest.
+
+## Guard after the old package is gone
+
+The séance needs `left-pad` as its oracle. Before removal, the old package's answers for a fixed seed are recorded in `seance/left-pad/golden.json` by `seance/left-pad/record-golden.mjs` (written by hand, using the séance's own generators) and replayed by `seance/left-pad/golden.test.mjs`. The live old-versus-new comparison stays and skips itself when `left-pad` is absent. To run it again: `npm install --no-save left-pad@1.3.0 && npm run seance`.
+
+## Known behavioural differences
+
+Found by running the séance against the real packages. `padStart` alone differs from `left-pad` as follows:
+
+| Input | Old package | Naive replacement | In the project-owned replacement |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| leftPad("abc", 6, "") | "   abc" (an empty fill becomes a space) | "abc" (an empty fill pads nothing) | Empty, null, undefined and false fill characters become a space, as before. |
+| leftPad("abc", 6, "xy") | "xyxyxyabc" (the whole fill is repeated once per missing character) | "xyxabc" (the fill is cut to the missing length) | The fill is repeated once per missing character, as before. |
+| leftPad("abc", 6, null) | "   abc" | "nulabc" (null is turned into the text "null") | null is treated like a missing fill character, as before. |
+| leftPad("abc", Infinity, "-") | "abc" (the length is truncated to 32 bits, so nothing is added) | RangeError: Invalid string length | Lengths that are not finite add nothing, as before. Lengths of 2^31 or more are outside what the séance compares: left-pad wraps them around. |
+| leftPad("abc", 5.5) | "undefinedabc" (a bug: a fractional length below 10 with a space fill reads a missing cache entry) | "  abc" | Not reproduced on purpose: the replacement pads, as every caller meant. The séance does not compare this case and pins the old answer in a separate test. |
+
+Decision (unattended run): adopt the bundle's replacement, which keeps the old answers, with one deliberate exception: the fractional-length bug (`"undefinedabc"`), which the replacement does not reproduce. The project never passes a fractional length (widths are the constants `QTY_WIDTH` and `PRICE_WIDTH` and the literal `8`), and its own tests do not need the successor's behaviour. The fill-related differences matter to the project because `options.fill` is caller-controlled, so the old answers are kept.
+
+## Risks
+
+- A behaviour the scan missed. The séance covers the default export only; the scan saw no other member.
+- Lengths of 2^31 or more are not compared.
+- Node below 22.12 cannot run the séance (not the production code).
+
+## Order of work
+
+Scan, spec, séance against the old code, mutant proof, switch, golden guard, removal.
