+# Requirements: Move off left-pad
+
+Generated by Necromancer. `left-pad` is **dead**; the chosen successor is `String.prototype.padStart` (native).
+
+## Why
+
+- Evidence: Deprecated on npm: "use String.prototype.padStart()" (npm)
+- Evidence: Abandoned: the latest release (1.3.0) is 8.6 years old and nothing shows it is still looked after (low OpenSSF Maintained score). (npm)
+- Evidence: The latest release (1.3.0) is 8.6 years old. (npm)
+- Evidence: OpenSSF Scorecard rates maintenance 0 out of 10. (scorecard)
+
+Why this successor: padStart is built into every supported JavaScript runtime.
+
+Version in use: 1.3.0 (from `package-lock.json`). No advisories were reported.
+
+## Where the project uses it
+
+The scan found one file that uses `left-pad`: `src/receipt.js`. It requires the default export once (line 3) and calls it 4 times with 2 or 3 arguments:
+
+| Call site | Call | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `src/receipt.js:34` | `leftPad(order.id, 8, '0')` | zero padded order number (a number, not a string) |
+| `src/receipt.js:44` | `leftPad('x' + item.qty, QTY_WIDTH)` | quantity column, default space fill |
+| `src/receipt.js:45` | `leftPad(money(cents, symbol), PRICE_WIDTH, fill)` | money column, `fill` comes from `options.fill` |
+| `src/receipt.js:51` | `leftPad(money(total, symbol), PRICE_WIDTH, fill)` | total line, same `fill` option |
+
+`fill` is caller-controlled (`options.fill`, default a space), so the fill can be any value a caller passes, including an empty string, `null` or a string longer than one character.
+
+## R1. Know how the project uses the dependency
+
+**User story.** As a maintainer, I want a list of every way the project uses `left-pad`, so that the migration covers all of it and nothing more.
+
+- R1.1 WHEN the project is searched, THE migration SHALL list every import, require and call of `left-pad` with the exported names used.
+- R1.2 THE list SHALL be saved in the repository so reviewers can check it against the diff. (It is the table above.)
+
+## R2. Same behaviour before and after
+
+**User story.** As a maintainer, I want proof that the replacement answers like `left-pad` for the way the project uses it, so that the switch is safe.
+
+- R2.1 THE project SHALL have a differential property-based test (a séance) that asks `left-pad` and the replacement the same generated questions over each API in R1.1.
+- R2.2 WHEN the two answers differ, THE test SHALL fail and print the input and both answers.
+- R2.3 WHERE both throw, THE test SHALL compare the kind of error, not the message text.
+- R2.4 THE test SHALL pass with the old implementation on both sides before any code is changed.
+- R2.5 THE séance SHALL be added to the project as `seance/left-pad/seance.test.mjs`, `seance/left-pad/replacement.mjs`, `seance/left-pad/README.md` and run with `npx vitest run seance/left-pad`.
+- R2.6 THE migration SHALL handle, or record as accepted, every known difference listed in the design.
+- R2.7 THE séance SHALL be shown to fail against a deliberately wrong replacement (the naive `String(str).padStart(len, ch)` swap).
+
+## R3. Use the platform instead
+
+**User story.** As a maintainer, I want the code to rely on `String.prototype.padStart` rather than a package, so that the project carries no package for it.
+
+- R3.1 THE code SHALL use `String.prototype.padStart` (through the project-owned wrapper `src/vendor/left-pad.js`, which keeps the old answers) where it called `left-pad`.
+- R3.2 THE project's supported runtimes (`engines.node >=18`) SHALL all provide `String.prototype.padStart`. (Node 18 does.)
+
+## R4. Remove the dead dependency
+
+**User story.** As a maintainer, I want `left-pad` gone, so that nothing unmaintained stays in the tree.
+
+- R4.1 THE project SHALL NOT declare `left-pad` in any manifest or lockfile after the migration.
+- R4.2 THE test suite SHALL pass after the migration.
+- R4.3 AFTER the removal, THE project SHALL keep a golden-file replay test that guards the new code against the old package's recorded answers.
+
+## R5. Safe to undo
+
+**User story.** As a maintainer, I want each step in its own commit, so that I can revert one step without losing the others.
+
+- R5.1 THE migration SHALL be made in small commits: test first, then the switch, then the removal.
