+# Séance: left-pad to String.prototype.padStart
+
+Generated by Necromancer (recipe `left-pad`).
+
+A séance asks the old package and its replacement the same generated questions and fails on
+any different answer. Run it before you switch, and keep it while you migrate.
+
+## Files
+
+- `seance/left-pad/seance.test.mjs`: the differential property test
+- `seance/left-pad/replacement.mjs`: the replacement to adopt (keeps left-pad's answers)
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+npm install --save-dev vitest fast-check left-pad
+npx vitest run seance/left-pad
+```
+
+## What it compares
+
+- The returned string, or the error class when the call throws (never the message).
+- Strings, numbers, null, undefined and booleans as the text; lengths that are integers, fractions, numeric strings, NaN and infinities; empty, multi-character and non-string fill characters.
+- Not compared: lengths of 2^31 or more (left-pad wraps them around).
+
+## Known differences
+
+Found by running the séance against the real packages.
+
+| Input | Old package | Naive replacement | In the generated replacement |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `leftPad("abc", 6, "")` | `" abc" (an empty fill becomes a space)` | `"abc" (an empty fill pads nothing)` | Empty, null, undefined and false fill characters become a space, as before. |
+| `leftPad("abc", 6, "xy")` | `"xyxyxyabc" (the whole fill is repeated once per missing character)` | `"xyxabc" (the fill is cut to the missing length)` | The fill is repeated once per missing character, as before. |
+| `leftPad("abc", 6, null)` | `" abc"` | `"nulabc" (null is turned into the text "null")` | null is treated like a missing fill character, as before. |
+| `leftPad("abc", Infinity, "-")` | `"abc" (the length is truncated to 32 bits, so nothing is added)` | `RangeError: Invalid string length` | Lengths that are not finite add nothing, as before. Lengths of 2^31 or more are outside what the séance compares: left-… |
+| `leftPad("abc", 5.5)` | `"undefinedabc" (a bug: a fractional length below 10 with a space fill reads a m…` | `" abc"` | Not reproduced on purpose: the replacement pads, as every caller meant. The séance does not compare this case and pins … |
+
